# Evidence artifacts are byte-exact captures: their recorded SHA256SUMS must
# survive clone/checkout. Disable ALL text normalization for them - pty logs
# legitimately contain CRLF, and autocrlf=input silently rewrote four D04b
# scripted-client.log blobs so the committed bytes no longer matched the
# recorded hashes (caught at commit ce8965e; a fresh clone would have failed
# the gate). Never remove without re-verifying every SHA256SUMS from a clone.
docs/migration/evidence/batch-c-artifacts/** -text
# Batch H captures include pty output, and a pty turns every newline into CRLF. Without
# this the committed blob differs from the working bytes the SHA256SUMS were taken over —
# the exact incident that made the committed-bytes check exist.
docs/migration/evidence/batch-h-artifacts/** -text
docs/migration/evidence/l-artifacts/** -text
